## High-level verdict

The changes since `31ca4e27` substantially implement the master plan through Phase 2A and the first coordinator-safety portions of Phase 2B. The code now has role-map enforcement, session-scoped spawn credentials, read-only capability gating, durable handoff/ledger/switch state, worker switch/fresh conversation, service/API/CLI/frontend surfaces for switch/fresh, an exclusive data-dir daemon lease, and a manager/database-backed orchestrator ownership safety layer.

The work is not complete for the full Target B plan. Phase 3A/3B limits, durable pause, manual continue, runtime failover bounds, and full orchestrator switch/fresh protocol remain open. Claude read-only enforcement also remains deliberately open, which blocks strict-project cross-harness orchestrator switch.

## Plan drift / master-plan amendments observed

The master plan itself changed in ways that match discovered capability constraints:

- Strict orchestrator changed from `claude-code` to `codex`, because only Codex currently advertises `read_only_enforced=true`.
- Implementor changed to `claude-code`, with Codex as the switch/failover rung.
- Pi/grok failover ladders were removed from the pasteable example because only Claude Code and Codex currently advertise `switch_supported=true`.
- Failover validation now requires `switch_supported` on both:
  - the primary binding of any role that has a ladder, because it is the switch source; and
  - every ladder rung, because it is a switch target.
- `limits` remains described as Phase 3 design intent but is explicitly not accepted by `domain.RoleMap` yet.

This drift is appropriate and documented, but it means old example maps with `_comment`, `limits`, Pi/Grok ladder rungs, or strict Claude read-only orchestrators are no longer valid.

